        "input": {
          "ruleId": "LOL-CAP",
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Make the liability cap mutual by adding a matching cap on Client's liability and a mutual consequential-damages exclusion.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] The cap in Section 12 protects TrueLink only and leaves Client's liability unlimited; our position is a mutual 12-month fee cap with a mutual exclusion of indirect damages. We have mirrored TrueLink's own cap language for Client rather than reopening the scope of TrueLink's cap, and confirm that Client's payment obligations, and each party's gross negligence, wilful misconduct, confidentiality breaches and indemnification obligations, sit outside the cap.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0077",
              "text": "IN NO EVENT SHALL CLIENT'S LIABILITY FOR ANY MATTER ARISING UNDER OR RELATED TO THIS AGREEMENT (OTHER THAN CLIENT'S OBLIGATION TO PAY FEES DUE UNDER SECTION 5, OR A BREACH RESULTING FROM CLIENT'S GROSS NEGLIGENCE OR WILLFUL MISCONDUCT) EXCEED THE TOTAL COMPENSATION PAID FOR HOSTING AND SUPPORT SERVICES OVER THE IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING 12 MONTHS PERIOD. NEITHER PARTY SHALL BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES ARISING UNDER OR RELATED TO THIS AGREEMENT."
            }
          ]
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "tool_use",
        "id": "toolu_01DutC6iYsB8ngvTuUxiu5bc",
        "name": "propose_redline",
        "input": {
          "ruleId": "INDEMN",
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Add IP infringement, breach of law, data-breach and gross negligence prongs to TrueLink's indemnity.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] TrueLink's indemnity covers only its own breach of the Agreement, so an infringement claim against us arising from the Interface (which TrueLink owns and does not warrant as non-infringing) would fall on Client. We have added the standard IP-infringement, breach-of-law, data-incident and gross negligence/wilful misconduct prongs.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0075",
              "oldText": "claim arising out of any breach by TrueLink of this Agreement or any failure by TrueLink in the performance of any of its obligations or agreements hereunder.",
              "newText": "claim arising out of (i) any breach by TrueLink of this Agreement or any failure by TrueLink in the performance of any of its obligations or agreements hereunder; (ii) any allegation that the Interface, the Hosting Services, the Support Services or any deliverable provided hereunder infringes or misappropriates any intellectual property right of a third party; (iii) TrueLink's violation of applicable law or any unauthorized access to or disclosure of Client Content, Credit Data or Client Proprietary Information caused by TrueLink; or (iv) TrueLink's gross negligence or willful misconduct."
            }
          ]
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "tool_use",
        "id": "toolu_01NZS8Q4VYFtorhQydVxdLum",
        "name": "propose_redline",
        "input": {
          "ruleId": "ASSIGN",
          "level": "fallback",
          "summary": "Add an M&A/successor carve-out, a reasonableness standard on consent, and confirm no change-of-control right for TrueLink.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] Section 15 allows affiliate assignments but blocks a transfer to a successor in a merger or sale of substantially all assets; we need the usual successor carve-out on notice and a \"not unreasonably withheld\" standard for other assignments.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0080",
              "oldText": "Neither party shall assign or transfer any of its rights under this Agreement without the prior written approval of the other party, except no such approval shall be required for an assignment to a financially responsible affiliate.",
              "newText": "Neither party shall assign or transfer any of its rights under this Agreement without the prior written approval of the other party, which approval shall not be unreasonably withheld or delayed, except no such approval shall be required for an assignment to a financially responsible affiliate or, upon written notice to the other party, to a successor in connection with a merger, acquisition, reorganization or sale of all or substantially all of the assigning party's assets. No change of control of Client shall give TrueLink any right to terminate, suspend or re-price this Agreement."
            }
          ]
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      },
      {
